# --- v2.0 additions ---

# Developer scratch. Reusable verification harnesses (audit.py, repair.py,
# assemble.py, golive.py and the rest of the release gate) live in the
# committed tools/ directory; this stays for one-off scratch and diagnostics.
_build/
_p_*.txt
_assemble.py
_append_probe.txt

# Backups left by tools/repair.py when it collapses a duplicated file.
*.bak

# Extracted JS that tools/vfrontend.py and tools/vreport.py regenerate on
# every run to node --check it; not source, nothing to track.
tools/app.js
tools/report_app.js

# Tier 2 full-array reference. Built locally by data/build_full_reference.py
# from ClinVar, the GWAS Catalog and CPIC. Far too large for GitHub, which
# rejects files over 100 MB, and it is fully reproducible from the builder.
data/reference.db
data/reference.db-wal
data/reference.db-shm
data/*.txt.gz
data/*.tsv.gz
data/_cache/
data/_build_freq.log

# The local SNPedia cache must NEVER be committed. SNPedia is
# CC-BY-NC-SA-3.0-US, so redistributing a harvested copy would relicense this
# repository. The harvester writes to ~/.dnainsight/ deliberately, outside the
# tree, but these patterns are a second line of defence.
snpedia_cache.db
*snpedia_cache*
.dnainsight/

# --- v3.0 additions ---

# External tools and reference panels. backend/external.py installs both into
# ~/.dnainsight/, deliberately outside this tree, so that a GPL-3.0 binary or a
# non-redistributable panel can never attach its terms to this MIT repository.
# These patterns exist for the same reason the SNPedia ones above do: the
# out-of-tree location is the design, and this is the second line of defence
# for the day somebody runs a builder with the wrong working directory.
tools_root/
panels/
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.bgz
*.bcf
*.bam
*.cram
*.crai
*.bai
panel.map
informative_markers.tsv
q_columns.tsv

# Reference panel build scratch. data/build_panel.py streams gigabytes through
# here and the outputs are fully reproducible from the builder.
data/_panel_scratch/
data/_panel_build.log
data/_pgx_build.log

# The CPIC allele table IS committed: it is CC0-1.0 and small. The
# reconciliation report is not, because it is a build artefact.
data/pgx_reconciliation.json

# Signed report manifests and the HMAC key that signs them. The key is a local
# secret: committing it would let anyone forge a manifest that claims to have
# been produced by this installation.
#
# The manifest pattern is SCOPED to the output directory on purpose. An
# unanchored *_manifest.json also swallowed data/tools_manifest.json, which is
# CC0 metadata that has to ship: it is the first file a licence auditor reads,
# and tests/test_builders_v3.py compares it against backend/external.py. A
# fresh clone would have failed that test with no obvious cause.
manifest.key
reports_output/*_manifest.json
reports_output/*_addendum_*.html
!data/tools_manifest.json

# Transfer scaffolding. Used once to move a release onto a workstation that has
# no direct file channel from the build environment. Safe to delete.
_xfer/
